  "narrative": "The newly delivered independent validation strongly supports H16. In the supplied dataset, feature_037=1 versus 0 is associated with much lower outcome_001 values, meaning stronger composite dependency: discovery signed effect +0.804 [0.742, 0.867], and independent validation signed effect +0.823 [0.732, 0.913] under the stricter validation interval. The validation lower bound is far above the 0.15 composite dependency-score-unit threshold, so H16 is accepted as a robust dataset-specific association. The claim remains association only: it does not establish causality, biological mechanism, or generalizability beyond this dataset.\n\nI also accept H39, the formal reversal of H15. The original H15 claim asked whether feature_010=1 was associated with stronger dependency and was rejected because R12 was strongly opposite. When the same binary contrast is formalized as feature_010=0 versus 1, the signed estimate is +0.829 [0.767, 0.891], again far above the threshold in the stronger-dependency direction. I therefore accept H39 as a dataset-specific marginal association: feature_010 negativity is associated with much stronger composite dependency. This is not yet independently validated and may partly reflect overlap with feature_037 or other measured predictors, so it remains active and is being followed by conditional checks.\n\nThe key unresolved issue is whether the two large associations are independent complementary markers or whether one is largely a proxy for the other. The next analyses are therefore prioritized on conditional robustness: H40 tests the feature_037 effect among individuals with feature_010=0; H41 tests the feature_010=0-versus-1 effect among individuals with feature_037=0; the new H43 tests the feature_037 effect among individuals with feature_010=1; the new H44 tests the feature_010 effect among individuals with feature_037=1; and the new H45 tests whether the feature_037 association is modified by feature_010 status. Together, these distinguish complementary associations from collinear or confounded marginal associations.\n\nH18 remains unresolved but scientifically close: feature_003=1 versus 0 has a signed estimate +0.139 [0.065, 0.213]. The point estimate is below the 0.15 threshold, although the upper interval crosses it. It should be followed only through conditional robustness, especially H42 among feature_010=0, because the large feature_010 effect may confound or mask smaller associations.\n\nNegative findings so far include the first two tested waves: feature_007, feature_058, feature_015, feature_024=level_002, feature_041, feature_031, feature_023, feature_054 contrast, feature_011 absence, and the tested marker-marker, feature_024-by-marker, feature_007-by-feature_038, and thresholded signature-moderated interactions do not support scientifically meaningful stronger-dependency effects at the 0.15-unit threshold. H4-H6 remain unresolved and deferred because exact continuous standardized-signature contrasts are operationally poor; they are superseded by thresholded signature-interaction designs rather than closed as rejected.\n\nThus, the current supported dataset-specific findings are strong marginal associations for feature_037 positivity and feature_010 negativity with stronger composite dependency. The most informative next analysis is the set of conditional and interaction contrasts for these two predictors, followed by validation of the strongest conditional result if the evidence persists across complementary cells.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 2 synthesis: Accepted H16 with independent validation: feature_037=1 vs 0 stronger composite dependency; discovery +0.804 [0.742,0.867], validation +0.823 [0.732,0.913], both >0.15. Accepted H39 (formal reversal of H15) as a strong dataset-specific marginal association: feature_010=0 vs 1 stronger dependency, discovery +0.829 [0.767,0.891]; not yet independently validated and may be collinear/confounded with feature_037. H15 remains rejected for the original feature_010=1 stronger-dependency direction. H18 feature_003 remains borderline unresolved: +0.139 [0.065,0.213]. Other tested predictors/subgroups and signature interactions are null or weak against the 0.15 threshold. H4-H6 remain unresolved/deferred because exact continuous signature contrasts are not operational; thresholded signature interactions were tested instead. Next priority: run or prioritize H40-H42 plus new H43-H45 to test conditional independence of feature_037 and feature_010: feature_037 effect when feature_010=0 and 1; feature_010 effect when feature_037=0 and 1; feature_037-by-feature_010 interaction. If effects persist across complementary groups and interaction is small, they are complementary dataset-specific associations. If effects collapse in the presence of the other predictor, one marginal association may be proxy/confounded. Then request validation for the strongest conditional claim, and follow feature_003 only if H42 gives a conditional effect above threshold or strong conditional evidence. All claims remain associations within the supplied dataset; no causal, mechanistic, or generalizable claims are supported."
